WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.540
Leah: Mental health concerns can be
painful and traumatic for all of the

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.870
family and can have a huge impact
both financially and emotionally.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.880
Also a child or young person’s
mental health problems, can

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.500
have real consequences for
others within their family.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.380
When a family member such as a child or
a sibling has mental health concerns, it

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.880
can be an extremely stressful time and
may in turn create health problems such as

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.769
headaches, loss of appetite, fatigue, and
insomnia for other members of the family.

00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:36.679
It may also cause cognitive and emotional
problems such as anxiety, depression,

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:43.400
guilt, anger, fear and confusion or
behavioural troubles such as changes

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.300
in attitude, and social withdrawal.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.249
Often family members develop
psychological or social problems of

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:54.960
their own, to such an extent that
they also need help and support.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.970
The consequences of poor mental health in
a family can further compound the mental

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.900
health of the child or young person.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.830
If they can see the effects their
mental health is having the family,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.679
such as loved ones becoming upset
and worried about them, they may

00:01:09.679 --> 00:01:13.800
try to remove themselves from family
life, so that normality can return.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.970
Children who are too young to fully
grasp the consequences of mental

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.630
illness can find it difficult to
understand why their sibling isn't

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.470
well or is acting unusually and may
tend to blame themselves and grow up

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.000
feeling different, lonely, and isolated.

00:01:29.709 --> 00:01:33.730
Ultimately this may lead to others
developing psychological, behavioural,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.339
and social problems of their own.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:41.250
Family life can become unsettled and
unpredictable causing a family member to

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:46.110
maybe leave their job, give up socialising
or following recreational pursuits.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.289
They may feel nervous about inviting
people into their home and find

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:56.510
it difficult to open up to people
about their relative's problems.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.599
It’s important therefor that we look
at the family as a whole when looking

00:02:00.599 --> 00:02:04.419
at the potential knock on problems
connected with Mental Health and look

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.650
to provide support options beyond
the immediacy of the person in focus

